BT /F2 22 Tf 48 558 Td (4. Event Processing And Alert Coalescing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 48 530 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 48 520 Td (Recommended Approach) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 48 503 Td (Use stream processing for real-time anomaly detection and alert coalescing.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 48 486 Td (Why) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 469 Td (- The 5 minute freshness requirement is explicit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 455 Td (- Raw event volume makes database-first aggregation expensive and operationally risky.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 441 Td (- Stream-time windows naturally model examples such as "50 anti-tamper disabled events) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 427 Td (  from the same agent in 10 minutes.") Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 413 Td (- Durable event logs allow replay when rules change or processors fail.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 48 399 Td (Coalescing Model) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 382 Td (- Partition by tenant and agent ID.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 368 Td (- Maintain keyed state for active anomaly windows.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 354 Td (- Emit alert transitions rather than every raw event.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48 340 Td (- Store raw event references for audit/debugging, not for every UI query.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 48 326 Td (Trade-Off) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 48 309 Td (This adds platform complexity, but it moves complexity into a purpose-built) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 48 292 Td (layer where latency, scale, and replay are controllable.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
